From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:22:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: PCI: google,gs201-pcie-cp: add the MSI page,
 isolation note

The modem link's MSI target is a fixed page of reserved RAM (Google's
cp_msi_rmem): the DesignWare MSI block terminates the MSI writes to it,
and the modem writes its boot stage into the same page. Describe it with
memory-region.

The PMU register is no longer only read: the controller sets the PHY
isolation again once the link is down.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 .../bindings/pci/google,gs201-pcie-cp.yaml           | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/google,gs201-pcie-cp.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/google,gs201-pcie-cp.yaml
index ae7416597..c3e58c9cf 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/google,gs201-pcie-cp.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/google,gs201-pcie-cp.yaml
@@ -82,7 +82,16 @@ properties:
       - items:
           - description: PMU
           - description: offset of the PHY isolation control register
-    description: PMU and the PHY isolation control register (read-only here).
+    description:
+      PMU and the PHY isolation control register. The PHY driver releases
+      isolation; this controller sets it again once the link is down.
+
+  memory-region:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description:
+      The modem's MSI target page. The DesignWare MSI block terminates the
+      MSI writes to it; the modem also writes its boot stage into the page,
+      so it must be reserved RAM.
 
   samsung,sysreg:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle-array
@@ -171,6 +180,7 @@ examples:
         interrupt-names = "ctrl", "msi0", "msi1", "msi2", "msi3", "msi4";
         phys = <&pcie_0_phy>;
         phy-names = "pcie";
+        memory-region = <&cp_msi_mem>;
         reset-gpios = <&gph0 0 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
         samsung,pmu-syscon = <&pmu_system_controller 0x3ec0>;
         samsung,sysreg = <&sysreg_hsi1 0x704>;
